<title>FRANCE: France to raise taxes on spirits - Mehaignerie.</title>
<headline>France to raise taxes on spirits - Mehaignerie.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Assembly Finance Commission chairman Pierre Mehaignerie said on Wednesday that increases in alcohol and tobacco taxes in the 1997 budget were expected to raise five to six billion francs.</p>
<p>He said that only strong alcohol -- 25 proof or above -- would be touched by the increase in taxes on spirits.</p>
<p>&quot;Wine and beer will not be affected,&quot; he told reporters.</p>
<p>Gasoline prices would increase only by 1.2 percent, the rate of inflation forecast for next year.</p>
<p>He said the commission members believed overall budget would set France on a path to growth.</p>
<p>&quot;This will put us back on the track to growth,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>He said the decrease in the deficit combined with income tax cuts &quot;make it a good budget&quot;.</p>
</text>
